{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrierEquiv"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.tlKernelPulled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.tlKernelPulled","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TLCarrierBridge.lean#L154-L164","doc":"**`tlKernel`, pulled back to the skein carrier — the point of this file.**\n\nIts type is `TwoSidedIdeal (QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke K q q⁻¹ n)`, which is *the same type as*\n`traceRadicalIdeal (wtrace q hq0 hq2 n) (wtrace_cyclic …)`. That this typechecks is what\ncloses bean `qou-jb7k`'s carrier mismatch.\n\n🛑 It does **not** say the two ideals are equal. That is the open problem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.skeinToTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.skeinToTL","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TLCarrierBridge.lean#L143-L152","doc":"**The TL quotient map, read on the skein carrier.**\n\n`heckeToTL` composed with `skeinCoxeterEquiv`, so its domain is the algebra carrying\n`wtrace` rather than the Coxeter-presentation algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.isTypeADiagram_AMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.isTypeADiagram_AMat","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TLCarrierBridge.lean#L137-L141","doc":"**`IsTypeADiagram` at `AMat`**, transported from `isTypeADiagram_coxeterFin` along\n`coxeterFin_eq_AMat`. This is the hypothesis `HeckeToTemperleyLieb` takes everywhere, and\nthe reason its results could not previously be read at `CoxeterCarrierEquiv`'s matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.coxeterFin_eq_AMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TLCarrierBridge.coxeterFin_eq_AMat","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TLCarrierBridge.lean#L129-L135","doc":"**The two type-A Coxeter matrices agree.** `HeckeToTemperleyLieb.coxeterFin` and\n`CoxeterCarrierEquiv.AMat` are the same function on `Fin n`; they differ only in the order\nof the two disjuncts of the adjacency test. ","signatureChunk":0}]}